; OpenXRVisibilityMask binds no property of its own — GDCLASS plus an empty
; _bind_methods (openxr_visibility_mask.cpp:37-38) — so layers is the sole
; key VisualInstance3D adds worth exercising here, at a non-default value:
; the default (1) Godot omits on save would exercise nothing.
;
; Parented under an XRCamera3D: Godot's own get_configuration_warnings
; (openxr_visibility_mask.cpp:70-75) warns a visible mask elsewhere, so this
; placement is what keeps the fixture's "zero warnings" claim honest rather
; than accidental.

